{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/criteria/overlay.py","reason":"logger + once-per-signature warn in _effective_routing_cached"},{"path":"src/rebar/_deprecations.py","reason":"step-1 registry row only"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/__init__.py","reason":":135 drop the deleted single-pass engine as a REVIEW_RESULT producer"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/code_review/assemble.py","reason":":9-15 rewrite the stale single_pass/lazy-re-export paragraph"},{"path":"docs/plan-review-gate.md","reason":":366 sentence"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_criteria_overlay.py","reason":"two tests"},{"path":"docs/config-reference.md","reason":"GENERATED artifact. The step-1 _deprecations.py row is the first-ever cfg-kind deprecation, so the previously-empty deprecated-alias table now renders a row. tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py::test_check_mode_clean_against_committed_tree fails until this is regenerated, so the ticket's own work compels editing it."},{"path":"scripts/gen_config_reference.py","reason":"Latent escaping defect this ticket is the first to exercise. _md_cell() escapes '|' but the deprecation (~:328) and tombstone (~:346) alias-table renderers applied it only to the final column, while the typed-keys table applies it to every cell. Both alias tables were always empty, so no prior change could trip it. The new row's replacement text contains a literal '|', which per GFM splits the 3-column row into 4 (cells split before inline code spans parse, so backticks do not protect it). Route name and replacement through _md_cell in both renderers."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py","reason":"Correct test_config_reference_reflects_cfg_deprecation_aliases to compare against gen._md_cell(dep.replacement) rather than the raw string, and add regression test_alias_table_escapes_pipes_in_name_and_replacement covering both columns. Mutation-checked: reverting the escaping turns the new test red."}]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"FILE_IMPACT","timestamp":1793410151148651211,"uuid":"d2916f8c-7ea7-480c-a192-29a0cc3b6da0"}